<title>USA: US weekly soybean crush 22,467,000 bushels -- NOPA.</title>
<headline>US weekly soybean crush 22,467,000 bushels -- NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 05/21/97    05/14/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 22,467,000  23,457,000    21,828,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  35,478	34,301	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,451,000  35,451,000    34,100,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,643,944  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   05/21/97    05/14/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   3,856,000   4,111,000     3,978,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    3,487,000   3,731,000     3,351,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,602,000   4,087,000     4,512,000</p>
<p> South Central    1,743,000   1,490,000     1,158,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,039,000   3,401,000     2,813,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,547,000   4,643,000     4,210,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,193,000   1,994,000     1,806,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	22,467,000  23,457,000    21,828,000</p>
